Hi all,

I'm very happy to announce that we've finally been able to upgrade the laye=
r=20
index at http://layers.openembedded.org to the latest revision on master,=20
incorporating quite a bit of work that's been going on for the past few=20
months. Improvements now visible:

* Patch tracking - each recipe detail page now lists any patches being appl=
ied=20
by the recipe along with upstream status for each - see attached screenshot=
=2E=20
You can click through to view/download the actual patch, and any URLs in th=
e=20
supplemental status text are also made into clickable links.

* Source tracking - remote entries in SRC_URI are now listed on the recipe=
=20
detail page and made into clickable links where possible - see attached=20
screenshot

* Link to inc files - there is now a link in the recipe detail page to any =
inc=20
files that a recipe includes as long as they are in the same directory, as =
a=20
shortcut to see the rest of the definitions for the recipe.

* Recipe list CSV export - there is now an "Export CSV" button at the top o=
f=20
the recipe list on the layer detail page. This currently includes the recip=
e=20
name and version - we could look at extending this, but note that the REST =
API=20
provides access to all of the information programmatically and may be bette=
r=20
suited for many applications that need this data.

* Site-wide notice support - admins can now add notifications to appear at =
the=20
top of the page across the entire site. This is useful in the case where th=
ere=20
is some problem with the update process or maintenance is going on as happe=
ns=20
from time to time.

* Bootstrap 3 - the UI has been updated to use Bootstrap 3 from version 2 t=
hat=20
we were using previously. This has made a fairly minor difference to the UI=
=20
(padding/spacing/fonts have changed a little) but has allowed us to tidy up=
 a=20
few things in the code.

* The "Base" layer type is no longer selectable for layer submissions. I=20
noticed people sometimes selected this erroneously; it's only applicable fo=
r=20
openembedded-core and meta-oe basically so that they show up at the top of =
the=20
layer list. Only admins can now select this type for a layer.

* Numerous other bugfixes, robustness improvements and code cleanups.

Thanks very much to everyone who has contributed to the layer index code up=
 to=20
now (and to BitBake / tinfoil, which we rely upon to extract the informatio=
n=20
from the metadata), but I'd like to give particular thanks to Michael=20
Halstead, Yi Zhao, Konrad Scherer, Robert Yang and An=EDbal Lim=F3n for mak=
ing=20
this upgrade possible.


Also integrated were the Recipe Reporting System (RRS) which powers=20
http://recipes.yoctoproject.org and other distro comparison support, but th=
ese=20
will take a bit more time to properly enable so I'll send out a separate em=
ail=20
with further details when they are ready.

As always, please let me know if you have any comments or notice any issues=
=2E=20
(I've already seen a few minor problems in the update logs so I'll be looki=
ng=20
into those.)

Cheers,
Paul

=2D-=20
Paul Eggleton
Intel Open Source Technology Centre

